            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Does the Matrix T7xe require a subscription?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              No. The Matrix app ecosystem handles workout tracking,
              entertainment streaming, and program logging, but every core
              function of the treadmill — speed, incline, built-in workout
              programs — works fully without ever creating an account or
              paying a monthly fee.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How does the T7xe compare to the Life Fitness T3?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              The T7xe has a stronger 4.0 CHP motor versus the T3's 3.0 CHP,
              a larger 22-inch-wide deck versus 20 inches, and a
              substantially bigger 15.6-inch touchscreen, all for roughly
              $1,000-$1,500 more. Both use fixed, non-folding frames and AC
              commercial motors. If you want the strongest spec sheet
              available at the entry commercial-adjacent tier, the T7xe
              wins; if brand pedigree and the lowest possible entry price
              into AC-motor territory matter most, the T3 is the cheaper
